{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/441731-a-newcommer-and-the-predator-s-taint-at-court","id":441731,"title":"A newcommer and The Predator's Taint at court","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-14T12:51:21-07:00","id":441731,"title":"A newcommer and The Predator's Taint at court","content":"So I'm STIng vampire for the first time in years and, well, I just noticed something. What happens when a new vampire shows up to court for the first time?<br /> <br /> After reading Predator's Taint, it turns out that whenever you meet a new vampire, you roll for it. It also said that you don't have to use it every time, but hey, I think it would be fun.<br /> <br /> So how would you handle someone new, someone low, like at 1 or 2, showing up to court for the first time? He's meeting 20 to 30 vampires. All at once. And many of them have a higher BP than him.<br /> <br /> What happens? Is there a system in place for this so that you don't have to roll 20 to 30 times?<br /> <br /> Here's my initial idea, as an ST:<br /> <br /> Skip the rolling altogether. The newbie falls into Rotschrek because he sees this going on and immediately, viscerally thinks: &quot;Oh shit, I am outside of my element.&quot;<br /> <br /> And also, two or three vampires of higher BP also flip out immediately. It's bound to happen over 20-30 rolls, right? So skip that and just make it happen. They immediately frenzy, and come at him, shouting some shit like HOWFUCKINGDAREYOUUUUUUUUUU because they perceive him as a new encroacher.<br /> <br /> Roll initiative. Let them get a few rounds of ass beating and shit wrecking before the fight gets broken up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2165-macai","name":"Macai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T13:00:23-07:00","id":441763,"title":"","content":"This kind of situation is why I'm so glad it's no longer automatic in second edition.<br /> <br /> In my old troupe we house ruled that when you're willingly going to court, you've psychologically prepared yourself for the fact that there are definitely going to be vampires there, and you might not know all of them. Predator's Taint rolls only happen when you unexpectedly encounter a new vampire, or during direct interaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T13:45:58-07:00","id":441826,"title":"","content":"My old Requiem ST made it a single roll for Elysium, rather than all encounters, and he gave us a +3 or something, because we'd psych ourselves up. The supplement <b>Invite Only</b> has material on this issue, I think. The first edition core actually suggests that you err on the side of <i>not </i>rolling for Predator's Taint unless it's dramatically interesting.<br /> <br /> Second edition gets rid of Predator's Taint and replaces it with Predatory Aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T13:59:12-07:00","id":441832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/441731-a-newcommer-and-the-predator-s-taint-at-court?p=441826#post441826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My old Requiem ST made it a single roll for Elysium, rather than all encounters, and he gave us a +3 or something, because we'd psych ourselves up. The supplement <b>Invite Only</b> has material on this issue, I think. The first edition core actually suggests that you err on the side of <i>not </i>rolling for Predator's Taint unless it's dramatically interesting.<br /> <br /> Second edition gets rid of Predator's Taint and replaces it with Predatory Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the tip. You got a page number?<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's page 55. Thanks anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2165,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2165-macai","user":"Macai","date":". 03-14-2015, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2165-macai","name":"Macai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:07:38-07:00","id":441917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/441731-a-newcommer-and-the-predator-s-taint-at-court?p=441763#post441763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This kind of situation is why I'm so glad it's no longer automatic in second edition.<br /> <br /> In my old troupe we house ruled that when you're willingly going to court, you've psychologically prepared yourself for the fact that there are definitely going to be vampires there, and you might not know all of them. Predator's Taint rolls only happen when you unexpectedly encounter a new vampire, or during direct interaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of like the idea of a debut routinely causing a huge ruckus every damn time. It's dramatic, you know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2165-macai","name":"Macai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T19:02:36-07:00","id":442080,"title":"","content":"I used it to good effect in one of my games. The two PCs were chained up and hooded, then brought before the assembled vampires at Elysium. Then the hoods were whipped off and the PCs freaked out. It highlighted how in over their heads they were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}